cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Mirobody: the AI-native health data engine"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmarks, please cite the ESL-Bench paper
  below. To cite a specific release, add its version and the DOI-free tag from
  https://github.com/thetahealth/mirobody/releases.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Theta Health, Inc."
    website: "https://thetahealth.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thetahealth/mirobody"
url: "https://docs.mirobody.ai"
abstract: >-
  Mirobody collects readings from labs, wearables and genetic tests, standardizes
  them to canonical codes (LOINC, UCUM, FHIR-recognized code systems), and
  answers questions over them with an agent. The resolver runs offline against a
  shipped LOINC 2.82 bundle with 49,253 multilingual aliases.
keywords:
  - health data
  - LOINC
  - UCUM
  - FHIR
  - terminology
  - clinical NLP
  - wearables
  - MCP
license: Apache-2.0
